Each element of {1,2,3,4,5,6} lies in exactly 5 of the 15 two-element subsets, because it can be paired with any of the other 5 elements.

So the sum of the 15 subset sums is 5 × (1+2+3+4+5+6) = 5 × 21 = 105.

\boxed{105}

Complete the square: (x−7)² + (y−24)² = 49 + 576 = 625, so the equation describes a circle with center (7, 24) and radius 25.

The maximum value of y on this circle is the center's y-coordinate plus the radius: 24 + 25 = 49.

\boxed{49}

Four digits in base 3 means $27 \le n \le 80$. Two digits in base 6 means $6 \le n \le 35$.

Both conditions hold exactly when $27 \le n \le 35$. The average of these consecutive integers is $\frac{27+35}{2} = 31$.

\boxed{31}

The congruence 8x ≡ 1 (mod p) has a solution exactly when gcd(8, p) = 1. For an odd prime p this holds, since 8 is invertible mod p. The only prime dividing 8 is p = 2, and for p = 2 the congruence reads 0 ≡ 1 (mod 2), which has no solution.

So p = 2 is the only prime for which the congruence has no solution, and the sum is 2.

